cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AITester in your research, please cite this software.
title: AITester — Logic-anchored Multi-agent Test Generation with Detection-first Protocol
authors:
  - name: AITester Contributors
    website: https://github.com/1956178912/AITester
version: 0.7
date-released: "2026-10-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/1956178912/AITester
abstract: >-
  A logic-anchored multi-agent system for Python unit test generation with a
  detection-first protocol ("red before green"), SpecIR specification oracles,
  paired attribution baselines (plain_llm / plain_llm_df), and M1 honest
  metrics (detection / repair / false-fix) adjudicated by held-out gold
  materials. The accompanying evaluation methodology — pooled multi-seed
  statistics with McNemar, Bayesian paired analysis, BH-FDR, and
  template-cluster sensitivity — is an integral part of the artifact.
keywords:
  - software testing
  - LLM agents
  - unit test generation
  - automated program repair
  - fault detection
  - specification mining
